    perf(numeric): interleave the dot products of the forward substitution
    
    Lu::solve takes 0.8 s of the 1.0 s of coarse-mesh solves in one 2A
    transport (perf, #0163). Each row's dot product is a chain of dependent
    additions, so the core waits on the add latency. Eight rows now advance
    their sums over the columns before the group together, each in its own
    order, so the results are the same bits (ADR-0188).
    
    Refs: #0163
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BtHJut79GtsihXA6Ta9jue

